(4926268, 713529, 97270, '<td valign="top">Where is the abstraction? What is it that you wanted to take away from the image in terms of recognizable structure?<br/> <br/>ETA (post voting): Thank you for your cross comment, I found it helpful. Although I have to admit judging abstract art is a very subjective skill. I really failed to see the abstraction in this image that you explained... all I could see was three recognizable objects. I learnt a lot about abstract images in this challenge, and must admit that my entry wasnt truly abstract either. I hope you appreciate the candor of people who actually commented on the images rather than just rating it low. Cheers to learning more...<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-09-03 01:19:09.</i></td>', 'Where is the abstraction? What is it that you wanted to take away from the image in terms of recognizable structure? ETA (post voting): Thank you for your cross comment, I found it helpful. Although I have to admit judging abstract art is a very subjective skill. I really failed to see the abstraction in this image that you explained... all I could see was three recognizable objects. I learnt a lot about abstract images in this challenge, and must admit that my entry wasnt truly abstract either. I hope you appreciate the candor of people who actually commented on the images rather than just rating it low. Cheers to learning more...', '2008-09-01 18:07:26.000000', '2008-09-03 02:19:09.000000', 1),
